// Title: Renamed Vmnat.exe Execution
// Sigma ID: 7b4f794b-590a-4ad4-ba18-7964a2832205
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2022-09-09 | Modified: 2023-02-03
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects renamed vmnat.exe or portable version that can be used for DLL side-loading
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/malmoeb/status/1525901219247845376
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_vmnat.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "vmnat.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "vmnat.exe"))
